        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `impact:ux-release-blocker` and `impact:ux-friction` as issue-only ClawSweeper impact labels.\n- Add a UX override rubric that promotes unrecoverable first-run/community UX blockers to `triagePriority: \"P0\"` plus `impact:ux-release-blocker`.\n- Require the prompt/schema/tests to preserve less-technical recovery guidance when terminal/config/log/manual-file recovery is currently required.\n\nCloses #386.\nRelated: openclaw/openclaw#75947.\n\n## Proof Boundary\n\nThis proves ClawSweeper can classify and label UX blockers. It does not claim the underlying OpenClaw first-run UX is fixed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm install`\n- `pnpm run build`\n- `node --test test/pr-label-policy.test.ts test/decision-parser.test.ts --test-name-pattern \"UX|priority|impact\"`\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- `node --test test/clawsweeper.test.ts --test-name-pattern \"UX|priority|impact\"`\n",
